[thin] Functional hook nose and insertion ramp. The 4.6 mm total hook height comprises a 1.6 mm tool-backed nose and a 3 mm pointed lead-in. Across the centered 5 mm blade entry, the 1 mm opening leaves a finite 0.6 mm nose above it. The tool-purchase roof and the adjoining insertion profile are functional parts of this specified hook. Physical insertion, release and repeated use are checked with the complete pointed sample.
alternatives: Increasing roof thickness within this height reduces the requested blade opening or steepens the insertion ramp; increasing total hook height also deepens its receiving pocket into the fixed roof stock. Filling the entry removes centered tool access. The 2.6 mm flat retaining overlap remains on each side of the entry.
